[UNIVERSAL VOLTAGE-BUFFERED RF TRANSCEIVER ARCHITECTURE]

 1. DECOUPLED POWER SHASIS HARDWIRING:
    - External Processing Host VCC (+5V Rail)  ---> YL-105 Adapter VCC Terminal
    - External Processing Host Ground (GND)    ---> YL-105 Adapter GND Terminal
    * Note: Onboard AMS1117 steps 5V down to 3.3V with transient damping buffers.

 2. HIGH-SPEED SPI PROTOCOL BUS MULTI-DROP INTERCONNECT:
    - YL-105 Adapter Socket CE Pin   ---> Host Processing GPIO Node (e.g., Uno D9 / STM32 PA0)
    - YL-105 Adapter Socket CSN Pin  ---> Host Processing GPIO Node (e.g., Uno D10 / STM32 PA4)
    - YL-105 Adapter Socket SCK Pin  ---> Host Hardware SPI Clock Node (e.g., Uno D13 / STM32 PA5)
    - YL-105 Adapter Socket MOSI Pin ---> Host Hardware SPI Data Out   (e.g., Uno D11 / STM32 PA7)
    - YL-105 Adapter Socket MISO Pin ---> Host Hardware SPI Data In    (e.g., Uno D12 / STM32 PA6)

 3. OMNIDIRECTIONAL SMA ANTENNA HARDWARE ALIGNMENT:
    - Secure the high-gain external SMA antenna tightly onto the gold-plated female connector thread.
    * Note: Guarantees full transmission power distribution over open fields without RF link mismatch.

